SCP-firmware v2.11.0's scmi_system_power module with CIX's change: for
the agents that may set the system state (PSCI, management), shutdown,
cold and warm reset and suspend only set the target of the PM's power
sequence (src/hsm: trigger_SD, trigger_RST, trigger_STR) and answer
success; the sequence runs once the answer is out.  No policy handler is
called and no notification is sent for them (CIX's neither).  Power-up
and other states take upstream's path.

And one fix: SYSTEM_POWER_STATE_NOTIFY answers NOT_SUPPORTED (as CIX's
does) when the module has no table of subscribers, which is the case
without an alarm for graceful requests; upstream wrote the agent's entry
through the null pointer.
